d with any mechanistic depth. | (e) The student has clearly misunderstood the max-min fairness algorithm entirely. The calculation '3 * 80 * 1.3' with a 'safety buffer' concept has no relation to max-min fairness - this appears to be network capacity planning terminology, not transport layer fairness. The student did correctly identify that total demand (240 Mbps) exceeds link capacity (200 Mbps), which is a prerequisite observation, but drew no useful conclusion from it. Part (ii) about 'overflowing into the safety buffer' is meaningless in this context and shows no understanding of how TCP or max-min allocation works.",
